# Intent: The first-run screens at finger size (owner review 2026-11-18, the physical standard in docs/design/screen-style.md; batch UX13d, audit docs/plan/screen-standards-audit.md). Back is 56 by 48 and Skip 72 by 48 in a header that ends at y 52, with the title between them; the language tiles are 96 by 56 in two rows; the name step is StackChan wide (304 by 48) over six 96 by 48 names; the brain step is three 304 by 48 tiles; the two hint lines that were under them (change it later, your voice stays home) are no longer drawn because they need two 16 px lines the glass has no room for (the last screen and the privacy step say the same); Got it on the privacy step and the last screen is 160 by 56 at the bottom, 8 px above the edge. Every target is 8 px from its neighbor and the header. The geometry lives in the core (maipai_firstrun_core.h) so its host test checks it. Display only: no safety, lock, cue, limiter or head-motion code.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_firstrun.cc, maipai_firstrun_core.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: each first-run step has Back and Skip a finger can press and tiles with a gap between them; Got it is easy to press; no text touches a button in any of the six languages.
# Kconfig: none

